  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Ford Edge?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. The Fuel Percentage signal (powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel) is listed for the Ford Edge, and you read it through the Telemetry API using a Vehicle JWT for the vehicle."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Ford Edge with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Ford Edge?",
      "a": "Idling is a listed event for the Ford Edge on a DIMO device. Query the Telemetry API segments resource with the idling detection mechanism, which finds periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range and requires a DIMO device."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Ford Edge mileage?",
      "a": "The Ford Edge reports an Odometer signal in km through a DIMO device. To get verifiable proof, POST to the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the signed statement through the Telemetry API attestations query."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Ford Edge, that data comes through a DIMO device, with coverage for model years 2011 and newer. The record lists this coverage as tested, not expected. Query it through the Telemetry API with GraphQL, or receive events through webhooks."
}
